              "id": "item_2",
              "command": "/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> docs/story/facts.md <<'EOF'\n\n# User-confirmed corrections — stop 1 completed\n\nSource for every item below: user's second substantive message, 12 October 2026. These answers supersede ambiguous CV wording above.\n\n- Public name: Ada Mensah. Public project name: Mosslink. Omit employer and employment dates from site and downloadable CV; current details/title not confirmed. No claim of current employment.\n- Personal work: wrote firmware, scheduled power states, built bring-up fixture. Colleague designed PCB and analogue front end. Do not say Ada owned sensor hardware design.\n- Battery: two-year projection from bench current readings and assumed reporting cycle; longest run 72 hours. No field endurance/weather testing supports two-year claim. Exact reporting interval unconfirmed and omitted.\n- Samples: forty engineering samples assembled; six bench tested. None sent to customers. No field pilot or launch. Do not imply Ada alone assembled or tested all samples.\n- Emissions: one preliminary check passed; full qualification programme unfinished. No certified/qualified claim or personal ownership of emissions result.\n- Radio problem: radio remained awake after failed transmission, seen in current trace. No cause, fix, timing or later resolution confirmed. No trace available.\n- Own fixture photograph and simplified power-state diagram permitted for public use. Photograph unavailable. Colleague's circuit diagram has no permission; exclude. The supplied two SVGs may serve as labelled explanations only, never photographs, original wiring, firmware, measured traces or results. Sleep/Measure/Transmit is a teaching sequence with no durations or current values.\n- Audience: firmware hiring manager. Desired understanding: how Ada connects code to a measurable signal.\n- Daily artifacts: state table, timing diagram, current trace; notes also list bench checklists. Bring-up means checking a new board's basic operation.\n- Expressed lesson: a firmware decision needs a physical observation; estimates and observed runs support different claims. This is a principle, not an all-problems-resolved/all-devices-tested claim.\n- End actions: email link to public example contact ada@example.com and download corrected printable HTML CV. No PDF invention, mail sending or delivery-test claim.\n- Mosslink only project; needs its own project page and main-story presence.\n- English, ordinary navigation, share preview, icon, useful missing-page page. No testimonials/blog/chat/translation/contact form. Legal/hosting-jurisdiction details deferred until publishing; no legal-compliance claim.\n- Local system fonts, supplied drawings or own explanatory geometry. No external purchase/download. No additional skill installation; user declined.\n- No old site or testimonials. Keep everything local; user decides publishing.\n\n## Remaining omissions, not blockers\nEmployment/title/dates, exact reporting cycle, radio cause/fix/timing/outcome, individual ownership of team sample/emissions results: unconfirmed and excluded. No extra facts requested because user explicitly instructed omission over guessing.\nEOF\nnode .agents/skills/storyfolio/scripts/scaffold.mjs site\"",
